            <ArticleTitle>Thalassemia intermedia and cavernous transformation of portal vein thrombosis in pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of a cavernous transformation of portal vein (CTPV) thrombosis accompanied by Thalassemia and thrombophilia during pregnancy that was successfully treated by low molecular weight heparin. The clinical presentation, diagnosis and the treatment are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
